# .trivyignore
#
# CVEs that have been reviewed and accepted as unfixable or false-positive
# for the AchaeanFleet container images.
#
# Format: each entry MUST be preceded by a 6-field structured comment block
# per SECURITY.md "CVE Suppression Policy" / "Required entry format":
#
#   # <CVE-ID>
#   # Category: OS | npm | python | other
#   # Rationale: <why it cannot be fixed here>
#   # Exploitability: <none | low | medium | ...> — justification
#   # Expires: YYYY-MM-DD  (max 90 days from approval; re-review before)
#   # Reviewer: @<github-handle>  PR #<number>
#   <CVE-ID>
#
# Reference: https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/#trivyignore

# NOTE (issue #760, 2026-08-23): the 6 claude-code bundled-npm entries
# (CVE-2024-21538, CVE-2025-64756, CVE-2026-26996, CVE-2026-27903, CVE-2026-27904,
# CVE-2026-23745) and the 14 stale-published-image aider python entries
# (litellm trio incl. GHSA-69x8-hrgq-fjj8, aiohttp CVE-2025-69223, pillow trio,
# protobuf duo, pyasn1 duo, urllib3 trio) were pruned after fresh local Trivy
# scans of rebuilt achaean-claude and achaean-aider images confirmed they no
# longer fire (claude-code 2.1.233 bump + aider-chat 0.86.2 with
# vessels/aider/requirements-security-overrides.txt). See PR history for the
# removed structured blocks. Reproducible check: run
# scripts/verify-trivyignore-prune.sh (rebuilds + scans without --ignorefile);
# the CI "Trivy scan vessel image (gate)" jobs are the authoritative gate.

# CVE-2026-39822
# Category: other
# Rationale: Go stdlib os.Root symlink-following, fixed in Go 1.26.5. Two vendored binaries in achaean-claude are still affected. (1) gitleaks v8.30.1 — the latest published release, pinned in ci/Containerfile — is built with Go 1.24.11; re-verified 2026-10-13 with Trivy 0.74.0 (`trivy rootfs` on the release tarball) and no newer release exists. (2) gh was installed unpinned from GitHub's apt repo; latest gh v2.102.0 (2026-09-30) is built with Go 1.27.1 and carries the fix, so the gh copy should clear on the next achaean-claude rebuild. PR #807 does not rebuild achaean-claude (Build Vessel Images is skipped), so the finding could not be re-scanned here and the entry is renewed rather than removed. yq was repaired independently by the v4.53.6 upgrade and no longer relies on this suppression. Tracking the remaining repair in #720/#779.
# Exploitability: low — os.Root traversal requires an attacker able to pre-place symlinks in directories gh opens via os.Root; gh runs as a developer CLI with no attacker-controlled filesystem input path in this vessel runtime. The gitleaks binary is a CI secret scanner with no untrusted filesystem input.
# Expires: 2027-01-11
# Reviewer: @mvillmow  PR #807 (re-review)
CVE-2026-39822

# CVE-2026-56864
# Category: other
# Rationale: golang.org/x/mod v0.38.0 vendored in /usr/bin/gh (GitHub CLI v2.96.0 in achaean-claude, built with Go 1.26.4) — malicious GOSUMDB arbitrary module content. Fixed in x/mod 0.40.0; gh v2.98.0 (2026-08-20, latest at re-review) shows no x/mod bump in its changelog, so no released gh build vendors the fixed version yet. Same binary/tracking as CVE-2026-39822 (issue #720).
# Exploitability: low — gh runs as a developer CLI inside the vessel and does not consume a GOSUMDB; module-verification code paths are never exercised against attacker-controlled sum databases.
# Expires: 2026-11-21
# Reviewer: @mvillmow  PR #TBD (issue #760 rescan)
CVE-2026-56864

# CVE-2026-56865
# Category: other
# Rationale: golang.org/x/mod v0.38.0 vendored in /usr/bin/gh (GitHub CLI v2.96.0 in achaean-claude, built with Go 1.26.4) — malicious GOPROXY sumdb forging. Fixed in x/mod 0.40.0; same unpatched-upstream situation as CVE-2026-56864 above.
# Exploitability: low — GOPROXY/sumdb verification paths are never exercised against attacker-controlled proxies in the vessel runtime context.
# Expires: 2026-11-21
# Reviewer: @mvillmow  PR #TBD (issue #760 rescan)
CVE-2026-56865

# CVE-2026-14257
# Category: npm
# Rationale: brace-expansion DoS — bundled with npm 11.18.0's dependency tree in achaean-base-* images. npm's bundled module tree cannot be overridden without forking npm; the fixed versions (5.0.8+) ship in newer npm releases than the pinned 11.18.0.
# Exploitability: none — brace-expansion input is npm-internal and hard-coded, never attacker-controlled in the vessel runtime.
# Expires: 2026-11-05
# Reviewer: @mvillmow  PR #766
CVE-2026-14257

# CVE-2026-69152
# Category: npm
# Rationale: second brace-expansion DoS — same bundled-npm dependency tree as CVE-2026-14257.
# Exploitability: none — npm-internal input only.
# Expires: 2026-11-05
# Reviewer: @mvillmow  PR #766
CVE-2026-69152

# CVE-2026-69192
# Category: npm
# Rationale: ip-address inconsistent parsing CVE — bundled with npm 11.18.0's dependency tree in achaean-base-* images (fixed in ip-address 10.3.1, ships in newer npm than pinned 11.18.0). npm's bundled module tree cannot be overridden without forking npm.
# Exploitability: none — ip-address input is npm-internal and hard-coded, never attacker-controlled in the vessel runtime.
# Expires: 2026-11-05
# Reviewer: @mvillmow  PR #746
CVE-2026-69192

# CVE-2026-73566
# Category: npm
# Rationale: tar 7.5.19 DoS via crafted long-path archive — bundled with npm 11.18.0's dependency tree in achaean-base-* images (fixed in tar 7.5.21, ships in newer npm releases than the pinned 11.18.0). npm's bundled module tree cannot be overridden without forking npm; the dagger/ lockfile override (tar ^7.5.21) covers only the CI pipeline, not the image.
# Exploitability: none — bundled tar input is npm-internal, never attacker-controlled in the vessel runtime.
# Expires: 2026-11-21
# Reviewer: @mvillmow  PR #TBD (issue #760 rescan)
CVE-2026-73566

# GHSA-f88m-g3jw-g9cj
# Category: npm
# Rationale: sharp@0.34.5 (transitive dep of cline@2.14.0 in achaean-cline vessel) inherits libvips CVEs CVE-2026-33327 etc.; fixed in sharp 0.35.0 but cline@2.14.0 pins the older range and no newer cline release resolves it yet.
# Exploitability: low — sharp is used only for local image processing in the vessel runtime; no attacker-controlled image input path reaches it.
# Expires: 2026-11-06
# Reviewer: @mvillmow  PR #746
GHSA-f88m-g3jw-g9cj

# CVE-2026-33818, CVE-2026-39821, CVE-2026-46600, CVE-2026-56853,
# CVE-2026-56858, CVE-2026-56859, CVE-2026-56860, CVE-2026-56862
# Category: other
# Rationale: golang.org/x/net cluster and golang stdlib compiled into the gitleaks binary (v8.30.1, pinned in ci/Containerfile). Fixed in Go 1.26.6 / 1.25.13 toolchains; no released gitleaks build vendors a newer stdlib. Re-verified 2026-10-13 with Trivy 0.74.0 against the v8.30.1 release tarball (`trivy rootfs`): every listed CVE still fires and v8.30.1 (2026-03-21) is still the latest published release. Correcting the original rationale: gitleaks is installed only into the achaeanfleet-ci container, which no Trivy image or filesystem scan covers, so these entries are defensive rather than load-bearing; they still hold if gitleaks is ever baked into a vessel image. This entry previously used a single non-conforming `# Expires:` line, so the expiry check in ci.yml never matched it; it is now in the required six-field form and is actively enforced. Same binary as CVE-2026-39822.
# Exploitability: low — gitleaks scans repository checkouts for secret patterns; no untrusted network input or attacker-supplied filesystem tree reaches it.
# Expires: 2027-01-11
# Reviewer: @mvillmow  PR #807 (re-review)
CVE-2026-33818
CVE-2026-39821
CVE-2026-46600
CVE-2026-56853
CVE-2026-56858
CVE-2026-56859
CVE-2026-56860
CVE-2026-56862

