# CVE-2026-93687
# Category: npm
# Rationale: braces 3.0.3 is the latest published braces release and npm
# registry metadata reports no fixed version; Trivy lists the finding with an
# empty Fixed Version, so the `security-dependency-scan` gate fires it. Chain is
# markdownlint-cli2@0.23.2 (exact pin) -> micromatch@4.0.8 -> braces@^3.0.3.
# Clearing it needs either a braces 3.0.4 release or a markdownlint-cli2 release
# that drops the micromatch dependency; neither exists. Verified 2026-10-13
# against registry.npmjs.org.
# Exploitability: low — braces expands glob patterns. The only consumer is the
# Markdownlint toolchain in ci/, and its inputs are repository-controlled globs
# from .markdownlint.yaml; no attacker-supplied pattern reaches it.
# Expires: 2027-01-11
# Reviewer: @mvillmow  PR #807
CVE-2026-93687

# CVE-2026-102276, CVE-2026-102278
# Category: npm
# Rationale: brace-expansion 5.0.9 is bundled inside the npm CLI's own
# node_modules at /usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/brace-expansion
# in achaean-base-node, achaean-base-minimal and achaean-base-python. npm's
# bundled tree cannot be overridden without forking npm. Fix floors are 5.0.10
# (CVE-2026-102276) and 5.0.11 (CVE-2026-102278). Verified 2026-10-13 against
# the published npm tarballs: 11.19.1 (the pin in bases/Dockerfile.*),
# 12.0.0 and 12.2.0 (current latest) all bundle brace-expansion 5.0.9, so no
# released npm clears the floors. Same bundled-npm situation as CVE-2026-14257.
# Exploitability: none — brace-expansion is called with patterns that npm itself
# constructs internally; no attacker-controlled glob reaches the bundled copy in
# these base images.
# Expires: 2027-01-11
# Reviewer: @mvillmow  PR #807
CVE-2026-102276
CVE-2026-102278

# CVE-2026-19534
# Category: npm
# Rationale: undici 6.28.0 is bundled inside the npm CLI's own node_modules at
# /usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/undici in achaean-base-node,
# achaean-base-minimal and achaean-base-python. Fixed in 6.28.1. npm's bundled
# tree cannot be overridden without forking npm. Verified 2026-10-13 against the
# published npm tarballs: 11.19.1 (the pin), 12.0.0 and 12.2.0 all bundle
# undici 6.28.0.
# Exploitability: low — the advisory needs a remote server to negotiate an
# unrequested WebSocket subprotocol. npm is used only to install from pinned,
# checksum-verified public registries in these images; no attacker-controlled
# registry host is contacted.
# Expires: 2027-01-11
# Reviewer: @mvillmow  PR #807
CVE-2026-19534

# CVE-2026-97687, CVE-2026-97689
# Category: python
# Rationale: urllib3 2.7.0 is not a standalone install in achaean-base-python.
# It is vendored inside pip 26.2.1 at
# /usr/local/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pip/_vendor/urllib3, which the
# digest-pinned python:3.14-slim base provides. Fixed in 2.8.0. 26.2.1 is the
# newest published pip, so no pip release carries the fix yet, and a vendored
# dependency only moves when upstream pip re-vendors it. Confirmed 2026-10-13
# against pip's vendor.txt at tag 26.2.1 (`urllib3==2.7.0`) and the Trivy
# target table, which lists pip-26.2.1, msgpack and setuptools as the only
# python packages in the image.
# Exploitability: low — pip is a developer CLI in the image. CVE-2026-97687
# needs a TLS-intercepting HTTPS proxy the operator must configure, and
# CVE-2026-97689 needs an attacker-controlled endpoint for pip to download from.
# Expires: 2027-01-11
# Reviewer: @mvillmow  PR #807
CVE-2026-97687
CVE-2026-97689

# CVE-2026-103111, CVE-2026-86145, CVE-2026-89157, CVE-2026-89161
# Category: OS
# Rationale: libpcre2-8-0 10.42-1 is pulled in by git in achaean-athena-tools,
# which installs git from the pinned Debian snapshot. The fixes are Debian point
# releases (10.42-1+deb12u1 and 10.42-1+deb12u2) that have not been published
# for bookworm yet, so no snapshot can carry them. Verified 2026-10-13 against
# the live archive: deb.debian.org/debian/dists/bookworm/main offers only
# 10.42-1, and debian-security bookworm-security carries no libpcre2-8-0 entry
# at all. The same holds at snapshot 20261012T000000Z, which is what this image
# pins. Per SECURITY.md this is the "fix not available in the base image's OS
# distribution" case. Revisit when Debian ships deb12u2 to bookworm.
# Exploitability: low — pcre2 is reached through git's regex handling on
# attacker-supplied repository content; the image runs git only against the
# pinned Athena revision fetch, not against untrusted repositories.
# Expires: 2027-01-11
# Reviewer: @mvillmow  PR #807
CVE-2026-103111
CVE-2026-86145
CVE-2026-89157
CVE-2026-89161

# CVE-2026-78667, CVE-2026-78669, CVE-2026-97031
# Category: other
# Rationale: Go stdlib and golang.org/x/net compiled into /usr/bin/gh in
# achaean-claude. vessels/claude/Dockerfile installs gh unpinned from GitHub's
# apt repository, so the image carries gh v2.102.0 (2026-09-30), the latest
# published release, built with Go 1.27.1 and x/net v0.58.0. The fixes need Go
# 1.27.2 (or 1.26.9) and x/net 0.60.0; no released gh build vendors them, and
# gh is distributed as a prebuilt binary we cannot rebuild. Same binary and
# tracking as CVE-2026-39822 / CVE-2026-56864 / CVE-2026-56865 above (issue
# #720/#779). Verified 2026-10-13 with Trivy 0.74.0 against the v2.102.0
# linux_amd64 release tarball (`trivy rootfs`), which reproduces exactly these
# four findings under the gate's own severity and ignore-unfixed settings.
# Exploitability: low — all four are denial of service. CVE-2026-78667 and
# CVE-2026-78669 need crafted HTTP Range headers or HTTP/2 SETTINGS, and
# CVE-2026-97031 needs multiple ECH outer extension references. gh is a
# developer CLI in this vessel talking to api.github.com; no attacker-selected
# endpoint, and request headers are generated by gh rather than supplied.
# Expires: 2027-01-11
# Reviewer: @mvillmow  PR #807
CVE-2026-78667
CVE-2026-78669
CVE-2026-97031

# CVE-2026-59723
# Category: npm
# Rationale: cline 2.14.0 is installed globally in achaean-cline; the fix needs
# cline 3.0.30 or newer, which is a major-version bump. The advisory covers
# cross-origin WebSocket hijacking of the Cline Hub dashboard /browser endpoint.
# The Fleet vessel never runs that dashboard: vessels/cline/Dockerfile sets
# AGENT_PROGRAM=cline and the agent runs headless, the Dockerfile declares no
# EXPOSE, and compose/ maps no port for the vessel. Revisit when the 2.x line is
# superseded or a backport reaches 2.x.
# Exploitability: none — no Cline Hub dashboard listener exists in this runtime,
# so the vulnerable endpoint is never bound.
# Expires: 2027-01-11
# Reviewer: @mvillmow  PR #807
CVE-2026-59723

# GHSA-rgj7-g3m4-5g8c, GHSA-wq5f-xc86-pv6w
# Category: npm
# Rationale: sharp 0.34.5 is a transitive dependency of cline 2.14.0 and
# carries libheif and librsvg advisories fixed in sharp 0.35.4 and 0.35.5. The
# cline 3.x line drops the sharp dependency, so the upstream remedy exists, but
# taking it now is a net regression: scanning the cline 3.0.71 dependency tree
# on 2026-10-13 with Trivy 0.74.0 shows it pulls simple-git 3.36.0
# (CVE-2026-102826, CVE-2026-102827, CVE-2026-102828) and @simple-git/argv-parser
# 1.1.1 (CVE-2026-102829) plus undici 5.29.0 (CVE-2026-12151, CVE-2026-1526,
# CVE-2026-2229) — seven additional fixable HIGH findings against the two
# here. Revisit when a cline 3.x release ships without those regressions.
# Exploitability: low — sharp is used for local image processing; this vessel
# runs cline headless against a workspace checkout, so no attacker-supplied
# image reaches libheif or librsvg.
# Expires: 2027-01-11
# Reviewer: @mvillmow  PR #807
GHSA-rgj7-g3m4-5g8c
